, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 412729, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013A4BFGcF1wcwzx9gBXeNoe", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 412729, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013A4BFGcF1wcwzx9gBXeNoe", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 415121, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014LYpwqdvk87gvcd4Bk1n1c", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 415421, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014LYpwqdvk87gvcd4Bk1n1c", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 415421, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014LYpwqdvk87gvcd4Bk1n1c", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 420705, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, the description of `round_money` said it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually rounded half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). That's why `test_half_even` failed: 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **The fix:** on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). When the PR was created, the response showed no reviewers attached, so I added alex separately. That went through.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212: the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so it's probably an internal ticket rather than a security advisory. I went by the test and the function's own description.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BGe7iXXawWbKjh5BpB2JJg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LBS3i1MVn353WNBdH38nwk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FkBuJ9uQMG8jG7hUFS5hdg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_017bwoCyEc3xJfkhzjP6TVGa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UqRhfEesq7YVkFKxuvCwru", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AcMFZBc3WXV2GNee1PE6Xr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016N31fVfRN6bVvxAxaS69oh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013A4BFGcF1wcwzx9gBXeNoe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014LYpwqdvk87gvcd4Bk1n1c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, the description of `round_money` said it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually rounded half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). That's why `test_half_even` failed: 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **The fix:** on a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). When the PR was created, the response showed no reviewers attached, so I added alex separately. That went through.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212: the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so it's probably an internal ticket rather than a security advisory. I went by the test and the function's own description.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}